## Pitfalls

- Never mistake a third-person summary, reaction, compilation, or AI recap about an influencer for the influencer's original source video. Probe the source style before rendering the batch.
- Never apply the faceless Daily Stoic narrator-and-illustration treatment to Viral Clip Radar; Viral Radar should look like a polished OpusClip-style direct excerpt.
- Never route faceless Daily Stoic by inbox ownership alone. The active destination is A F (`fareed320`), even though source newsletters may also come from `fareed320@gmail.com`; enforce the registered token and expected A F channel ID.
- Do not let cron publish the same fixed title/video every day.
- Do not use the old fixed NASA-only Viral Radar lane as the default unless no reviewed fresh clips are available.
- Do not treat missing metrics credentials as content performance data.
- Keep cron prompts self-contained because scheduled runs do not inherit chat context.
- Do not leave creative content jobs as `no_agent=true` script-only jobs when the user expects fresh research and decision-making each run; use deterministic scripts only as substeps inside an agent-driven cron.
